+
+### Dots custom build: external syntax themes
+
+This 1.28.2+dots.1 build also accepts a `.tmTheme` file in a custom theme's `syntax` field, for example `syntax = "dots.tmTheme"`. Relative paths are resolved beside the external theme TOML, or beside config.toml for embedded named themes (including names selected by CLI/environment). Absolute paths and symlinked files are supported. Built-in syntax names retain their existing behavior.
+
+A selected unreadable or malformed syntax file stops startup with an error in both TUI and inline modes. Unselected files are not loaded. Syntax colors are loaded once per launch and retained across document reload, resize and theme-picker cancellation; start a new Leaf process after publishing new colors.
